("A patient takes in 80 g protein a day and has a 24-hour urine urea nitrogen of 14 g. Adding 4 g for other losses, what is the nitrogen balance?",
 "-5.2 g", ["-1.2 g", "+5.2 g", "-3.2 g"],
 "Nitrogen intake is protein / 6.25 = 80 / 6.25 = 12.8 g. Losses are 14 + 4 = 18 g, so the balance is 12.8 - 18 = -5.2 g, a catabolic state. Leaving out the 4 g of other losses gives -1.2 g, and adding only 2 g gives -3.2 g."),
